Demonstration link: https://youtu.be/wgwzzkYciXU

This project is a simple C++ console-based Student Management System that connects to a PostgreSQL database using the libpqxx library.

It allows users to:

    Display all current students

    Add a new student

    Update a student’s email address

    Delete a student record

The program is menu-driven and loops until the user chooses to exit.

Requirements:
    Component	        Description
    CLion IDE	        Used for building and running the project
    Compiler	        Microsoft Visual Studio (MSVC)
    CMake	            Managed automatically by CLion
    PostgreSQL	        Installed locally (v14 or later recommended)
    pgAdmin 4	        For database and table creation
    vcpkg	            For dependency management
    libpqxx	            PostgreSQL C++ client library (libpqxx:x64-windows)


Database Setup:

1) Open pgAdmin 4 and connect to your local PostgreSQL server.

2) Create a new database: CREATE DATABASE COMP3005_A3_Q1;

3) Open the SQLQuery.txt file, copy and paste the queries to your PostGreSQL query tool to create table and initialize data.

4) Change the initDB() in main.cpp so that it matches your database info.


Installation and setup:
1)Download and install CLion

2)Open PowerShell or Command Prompt and run:
    vcpkg integrate install
    vcpkg install libpqxx:x64-windows

3)Download and install MSVC compiler from: https://visualstudio.microsoft.com/downloads/

4)Configure CLion:
    In the setting -> Build, Execution, Deployment -> Toolchain -> choose Visual Studio (MSVC)
    In the setting -> Build, Execution, Deployment -> CMake Options: -DCMAKE_TOOLCHAIN_FILE=C:/vcpkg/scripts/buildsystems/vcpkg.cmake


Build:
Open the project folder -> Click Build -> Build Project

Run:
Then click "run" icon to run the program.


